'。可能是个bug。我可以尝试不提供type_filter参数，只传action。让我再试一次，这次不包含type_filter。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2358, "output_tokens": 363, "latency_ms": 10156.821299984585, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户提醒我已进入 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段。当前可用的工具有 manage_alarms 和 manage_points（仅 list_points）。用户要求给 TI-201 设置 HH alarm 和 LL alarm，分别在 100 和 10，priority 设为 high。TI-201 很可能是一个模拟量点（analog point），因为 HH 和 LL 通常用于模拟量报警。首先我需要确认 TI-201 这个点是否存在，以及它的类型。我可以用 manage_points 的 list_points 来查询。但之前尝试 list_points 时遇到了 schema 错误，因为 type_filter 参数不允许为 null。不过，这次我可以指定类型为 \"analog\" 来过滤。先试试看。如果点不存在，可能需要先创建点，但用户没有要求创建点，只是要求配置报警。不过，根据工具描述，create_analog_alarm 要求 \"tag\" 是一个已存在的模拟量点。所以需要确认点是否存在。如果点不存在，可能需要先创建点，但当前阶段没有创建点的工具（list_points 只能查询）。我可以尝试查询模拟量点列表，看看 TI-201 是否在其中。如果不在，我可能需要告知用户点不存在，或者切换到其他阶段来创建点。但根据工作流上下文，当前阶段是 CONFIG_ALARM，可切换的下一阶段有 BIND_POINTS 等。不过，用户明确要求配置报警，我应该先尝试查询。用 list_points，type_filter 为 \"analog\"。"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4098, "output_tokens": 275, "latency_ms": 7809.848000004422, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要创建两个报警：一个HH（高高）报警在100，一个LL（低低）报警在10，针对TI-201标签，优先级都是high。\n\n根据当前可用的工具，manage_alarms支持create_analog_alarm动作。我需要为TI-201创建两个模拟量报警：一个用于高高限（HH），一个用于低低限（LL）。\n\n对于HH报警：high_limit=100，low_limit=null（或不设置），因为只关心高限。对于LL报警：low_limit=10，high_limit=null。两者优先级都是high。\n\n我需要为每个报警提供唯一的id。例如：alarm_TI201_HH 和 alarm_TI201_LL。\n\n现在调用manage_alarms来创建这两个报警。先创建HH报警。"}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4447, "output_tokens": 303, "latency_ms": 5945.320700004231, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想要给TI-201设置HH报警（100）和LL报警（10），优先级都是high。之前尝试调用manage_alarms创建HH报警时，参数类型出错。错误信息是：\"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"。可能是low_limit参数需要数字，而我传递了字符串\"None\"？实际上JSON schema中low_limit可以是数字或null。我应该传递null而不是字符串\"None\"。在JSON中，null是关键字，但在Python的参数中，可能需要使用None？但工具调用是通过JSON传递的，所以应该使用JSON null。在函数调用中，对于可空参数，我可以直接不传递该参数，或者传递null。让我重新尝试创建HH报警，这次不传递low_limit参数，或者传递null。先尝试不传递low_limit，因为它是可选的，有默认值null。但根据schema，low_limit是anyOf: [number, null]，默认null。所以可以不传递该参数。试试看。"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4824, "output_tokens": 271, "latency_ms": 5185.985399992205, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "看起来manage_alarms的schema有问题。错误信息显示\"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"。这表明系统期望low_limit是一个数字，但可能收到了null或者某种字符串。让我检查一下schema：low_limit是anyOf: [{type: number}, {type: null}]，默认是null。这应该是正确的。但错误表明系统可能将null解析为字符串了。\n\n也许我需要明确传递low_limit为null而不是省略它？或者传递0？对于HH报警，low_limit应该为null或者不设置。让我尝试传递low_limit为null。在JSON中，null需要写为null。在调用中，我应该传递low_limit: null。但是之前的调用省略了low_limit参数，可能系统默认传递了字符串\"null\"。让我显式传递null。"}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5169, "output_tokens": 131, "latency_ms": 3654.9383000237867, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The issue seems to be that the tool expects `low_limit` to be a number or null, but when passing `None` in the JSON, it might be getting interpreted as a string. Let me try omitting the `low_limit` parameter entirely for the HH alarm since it has a default of null."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5374, "output_tokens": 377, "latency_ms": 8359.756899997592, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The error message says \"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". This suggests that the system is receiving a string value for low_limit, possibly the string \"null\" or \"None\" instead of an actual null value. In JSON schema, null should be a proper JSON null value.\n\nLet me try with explicit JSON null. In the tool call, I need to pass actual null, not the string \"None\". Looking at the schema:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}\n```\n\nSo it should accept either a number or null. The problem might be that I'm passing \"None\" as a string. Let me try without the parameter at all (since it has a default of null). Wait, I already tried that and got the same error.\n\nActually, looking at the error more carefully: \"unable to parse string as a number\" - it's trying to parse something as a number but getting a string. Maybe the tool implementation has a bug where it's trying to parse \"null\" as a number?\n\nLet me try passing low_limit as 0 (zero) instead, and see if that works. For HH alarm, low_limit isn't really used anyway. Let me also try with deadband explicitly."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 28592, "output_tokens": 2150, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 57130.988299963064}, "judge": null}
