ens": 612, "latency_ms": 18217.832700000145, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想要创建一个反应釜综合监控方案，需要：新建画面、创建三个点位（温度、压力、液位）、绑定到画面的罐子和仪表上，最后下发验证。\n\n但根据当前阶段（VALIDATE），可用的工具只有 list 类操作（list_pages, list_history, list_scripts, list_points）和 validate_project/show_deployment_status。这些工具无法创建点位、创建页面或绑定控件。用户的需求需要进入 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段，那里可能有更多功能（如创建点位、页面等）。\n\n根据行为准则第5条：若当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，可以在回复的纯文本中包含 \"next_state: 阶段名\" 来切换到【可切换的下一阶段】中的合适阶段。可切换的下一阶段包括 ANALYZE_INTENT、DEPLOY、DONE。用户的需求属于设计/配置阶段，应该切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT。\n\n不过，我可以先使用当前可用的工具来检查现有配置，但用户明确要求新建，所以直接切换可能更合适。\n\n我应该先说明当前阶段的限制，然后切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT。但根据行为准则，我需要先尝试用可用工具满足需求吗？用户要求“建”和“新建”，这属于创建操作，当前工具无法完成。因此，我应该切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT。\n\n那么，我会在回复中包含 \"next_state: ANALYZE_INTENT\"，然后结束。但根据准则，完成任务后必须明确告知用户，并在回复中包含 \"next_state: DONE\"。然而，任务并未完成，只是阶段切换。所以我应该说：由于当前阶段无法完成创建操作，需要切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段。\n\n让我这样回复：说明当前阶段只有查询和验证工具，无法创建点位和页面，需要切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段来处理设计需求。然后包含 \"next_state: ANALYZE_INTENT\"。\n\n但为了更全面，也许我可以先列出现有的点位和页面，看看是否已经存在相关配置。不过用户明确要求新建，所以可能不需要。\n\n我决定先调用 list_points 和 list_pages 来了解当前状态，但这不是必需的。用户可能期望我们直接开始创建。然而，作为助手，我们应该先了解现状。但根据行为准则，如果信息不足，应先调用查询类工具或向用户确认。这里用户需求很明确，但我们可以先查询以了解现状。\n\n那么，我会并行调用 list_points 和 list_pages，然后根据结果决定下一步。但当前阶段不允许创建，所以最终还是需要切换阶段。\n\n开始吧。"}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1843, "output_tokens": 340, "latency_ms": 12375.113399990369, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "当前项目状态：点位 0 个，页面 0 个，是空项目。\n\n要完成反应釜综合监控方案，需要：\n1. 创建三个点位（温度、压力、液位）\n2. 新建一个监控画面（页面）\n3. 将点位绑定到画面中的罐子和仪表控件上\n4. 验证并下装\n\n但当前 VALIDATE 阶段仅提供查询和验证工具，无法创建点位或页面。需要切换到设计阶段来执行创建和绑定操作。\n\nnext_state: ANALYZE_INTENT", "reasoning": "当前项目中没有点位，也没有页面。用户需要创建反应釜综合监控方案，这完全是从零开始。在 VALIDATE 阶段，我们只能查看点位和页面，无法创建。因此，需要切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段，那里可能有创建点位、页面、绑定等工具。\n\n根据行为准则第5条，我可以在回复的纯文本中包含 \"next_state: 阶段名\" 来切换。我会在回复中说明：当前项目为空，需要创建点位和页面，而当前阶段只有查询工具，因此切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段来处理设计需求。\n\n那么，回复内容如下：先概述当前状态（无点位、无页面），然后说明需要创建三个点位和一个页面，并进行绑定，最后验证下装。由于当前阶段工具不足，切换到 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段。包含 \"next_state: ANALYZE_INTENT\"。\n\n现在生成回复。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2237, "output_tokens": 815, "latency_ms": 23754.658900026698, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户已进入 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段。当前可用工具包括：manage_alarms, manage_bindings, manage_pages, manage_points。这些工具可以完成用户的需求：创建点位、创建页面、绑定点位到控件，最后还需要验证和下装。但用户最后提到\"最后下发验证\"，这需要使用 validation 工具，而 validation 在当前阶段不可用（只在 VALIDATE 和 DEPLOY 阶段可用）。不过，我可以先完成创建和绑定，然后根据行为准则，当需要其他阶段的工具时，在回复中包含 next_state 来切换。\n\n首先，我需要创建三个点位：温度、压力、液位。使用 manage_points 的 create_point 动作。需要为每个点位提供参数：名称、数据类型、描述、单位等。温度可能是浮点数，单位摄氏度；压力可能是浮点数，单位MPa；液位可能是浮点数，单位百分比或米。\n\n然后，创建一个页面用于反应釜监控。使用 manage_pages 的 create_page 动作，需要提供名称和类型（如 Process）。\n\n接下来，需要将点位绑定到画面的罐子和仪表上。但绑定需要知道具体的控件 ID。我还没有创建控件，页面创建后可能是空的。根据 manage_bindings 工具，需要提供 source_point_id、target_type、target_id、property。target_type 可能是 \"control\"，target_id 是控件 ID，property 是控件的属性（如温度显示值）。但首先需要有控件。可能页面创建后会有默认控件？或者需要先创建控件？用户说\"绑到画面的罐子和仪表上\"，可能页面创建后会有默认的罐子和仪表控件？不确定。\n\n让我先创建点位和页面，然后再处理绑定。可能需要查询页面创建后的控件列表。manage_pages 有 get_page_details 可以查看页面详细信息。\n\n先并行创建三个点位和页面。但绑定需要点位 ID 和控件 ID，所以需要顺序执行。\n\n让我先创建三个点位。每个点位需要唯一名称。使用以下参数：\n- 温度：name=\"Temperature\", data_type=\"float\", description=\"反应釜温度\", unit=\"°C\", min=0, max=200\n- 压力：name=\"Pressure\", data_type=\"float\", description=\"反应釜压力\", unit=\"MPa\", min=0, max=10\n- 液位：name=\"Level\", data_type=\"float\", description=\"反应釜液位\", unit=\"%\", min=0, max=100\n\n然后创建页面：name=\"Reactor Monitoring\", type=\"Process\"\n\n然后获取页面详情，查看有哪些控件可用，再将点位绑定到相应控件属性。\n\n开始执行。"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3195, "output_tokens": 604, "latency_ms": 19681.76880001556, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "工具调用出错了，提示需要 `tag` 和 `type` 字段。看来点位的定义必须包含这两个字段。`tag` 应该是点位的标识符（唯一名称），`type` 可能是指点位的类型（如模拟量、数字量等）。需要查看工具的 JSON Schema 来确认具体要求。但工具列表里没有 schema 信息，只能从错误信息推断。\n\n我需要修正点位定义，添加 `tag` 和 `type` 字段。`tag` 可以设为 \"Temperature\"、\"Pressure\"、\"Level\"。`type` 可能是 \"analog\" 或 \"float\"，但错误信息显示 `type` 是必填项，可能是一个枚举值。也许是 \"analog\"、\"digital\"、\"string\" 之类的。先试试 \"analog\"。\n\n另外，`name` 和 `description` 可能还需要吗？`tag` 可能是唯一标识符，`name` 是显示名称。先尝试如下：\n\n点位1: tag: \"Temperature\", type: \"analog\", name: \"反应釜温度\", description: \"反应釜温度\", unit: \"°C\", min: 0, max: 200\n点位2: tag: \"Pressure\", type: \"analog\", name: \"反应釜压力\", description: \"反应釜压力\", unit: \"MPa\", min: 0, max: 10\n点位3: tag: \"Level\", type: \"analog\", name: \"反应釜液位\", description: \"反应釜液位\", unit: \"%\", min: 0, max: 100\n\n再试一次。"}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3942, "output_tokens": 246, "latency_ms": 6170.868600020185, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "还是同样的错误。可能是参数传递方式不对。工具调用格式应该是 `{\"action\": \"create_point\", \"point\": {...}}`。但错误提示 \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\"，这意味着在 point 对象中，tag 和 type 是必需的。我已经提供了，但为什么还报错？可能是我需要用不同的参数名。让我查看工具定义：manage_points 的 create_point 需要 \"point\" 参数。在 schema 中，point 对象需要哪些字段？工具描述没有详细说明，但错误信息表明需要 tag 和 type。也许我需要提供完整的 point 对象，包括所有必需字段。可能还有其他必需字段，如 \"dataType\" 而不是 \"type\"。试试 \"dataType\": \"float\"。或者可能是 \"pointType\"。先尝试最简单的：只提供 tag 和 type。`{\"tag\": \"Temperature\", \"type\": \"analog\"}`。试试看。"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4257, "output_tokens": 391, "latency_ms": 15601.102400047239, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户说\"你已进入 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段，请使用当前可用工具继续完成任务。\" 这似乎是系统提示，但工具调用仍然失败。我需要重新审视工具定义。查看manage_points的定义：它有一个参数action和point。point是一个对象，但schema没有详细说明。错误信息说\"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\"，这意味着在create_point action中，point对象必须包含tag和type字段。但我已经提供了，为什么还报错？可能是JSON格式问题？让我检查调用格式：我传入了{\"tag\": \"Temperature\", \"type\": \"analog\"}，这应该是正确的。\n\n也许point参数需要包装在更大的结构里？不，工具定义明确显示point是顶级参数。或者可能是action和point的层级问题？工具调用应该是：{\"action\": \"create_point\", \"point\": {...}}。我正是这样做的。\n\n或许type字段的值需要是特定的枚举？\"analog\"可能不对，可能是\"float\"、\"real\"、\"int\"、\"digital\"等。但错误信息说\"Field required\"，意思是字段缺失，而不是值错误。这很奇怪，因为我已经提供了字段。\n\n让我尝试完全不同的方法：也许我需要先列出可用的点位类型？但list_points已经返回空。或者查看是否有其他工具可以获取schema？没有。\n\n也许我需要先创建页面，然后再创建点位？但用户需求是创建三个点位和一个页面。\n\n让我尝试创建页面，看看是否能成功，从而验证工具是否正常工作。使用manage_pages的create_page action。"}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4717, "output_tokens": 222, "latency_ms": 9662.509299989324, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我注意到工具返回的错误信息是\"create_page.id: Field required\"和\"create_page.name: Field required\"。这意味着在调用create_page时，需要在顶层提供id和name字段，而不是嵌套在page对象中。让我重新阅读工具定义。\n\n查看manage_pages工具的参数定义：\n- 对于create_page操作，需要一个object，包含action（const: \"create_page\"），以及可选的id和name。\n\n确实，schema显示：create_page需要一个对象，包含action: \"create_page\"，以及id和name字段（都是字符串）。所以我不应该将id和name嵌套在page对象中，而是应该直接作为顶层参数。\n\n同样，对于create_point操作，需要action: \"create_point\"，以及tag和type字段作为顶层参数。\n\n让我尝试正确的格式。首先创建点位。"}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5008, "output_tokens": 318, "latency_ms": 14967.020499985665, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要仔细看看工具的参数定义。从工具列表看，每个工具的参数schema都不同。manage_points的create_point需要point对象，但工具定义里point对象有具体的属性要求。我看到错误是\"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\"，说明tag和type是point对象内部的必填字段。但我之前已经提供了这些字段，为什么还报错？\n\n让我重新读一下工具定义：manage_points工具的参数是一个oneOf，其中create_point对象需要action为\"create_point\"，以及一个point属性。point属性本身应该是一个对象，包含tag和type等字段。但错误信息显示的是\"create_point.tag\"和\"create_point.type\"，这意味着工具期望tag和type直接在顶层，而不是在point对象里？\n\n不对，再看工具定义：create_point的properties里有action和point，point是一个对象。但错误信息说\"create_point.tag: Field required\"，这看起来像是工具把point对象展开到了顶层。也许工具的实现是期望tag和type作为直接参数，而不是嵌套在point对象里？\n\n让我尝试不同的方式：直接传递tag和type作为顶层参数，不嵌套在point对象里。但根据schema，应该用point对象。不过既然报错，试试直接传递。"}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5395, "output_tokens": 552, "latency_ms": 10394.403500016779, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I'm getting schema errors repeatedly. Let me look at the function schema more carefully.\n\nFor `manage_points` with `create_point`:\n- The action should be \"create_point\"\n- The schema says it expects a parameter called \"point\" which is an object with properties: tag, type\n\nBut the error says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\"\n\nLooking at the schema definition for `create_point` action:\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": {\"const\": \"create_point\"},\n  \"point\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"tag\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n      \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"tag\", \"type\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait, but the error message format \"create_point.tag\" suggests the schema validation is expecting the fields at a different level. Let me try passing the point object with the tag and type fields directly.\n\nActually, looking at the schema more carefully:\n```json\n{\"type\": \"object\", \"title\": \"create_point\", \"properties\": {\"action\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"const\": \"create_point\"}, \"point\": {\"properties\": {\"tag\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"tag\", \"type\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"required\": [\"action\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}\n```\n\nSo the structure should be:\n```\n{\n  \"action\": \"create_point\",\n  \"point\": {\n    \"tag\": \"...\",\n    \"type\": \"...\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBut I'm passing this and getting the error. Let me try without the nested structure and see if the tool expects flat parameters.\n\nWait, looking at my call:\n```\n{\"action\": \"create_point\", \"point\": {\"tag\": \"Temperature\", \"type\": \"analog\"}}\n```\n\nThis should be correct according to the schema. But the error says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\" which suggests it's looking for tag and type at the top level under \"create_point\".\n \nMaybe the error message format is indicating the path differently. The validation might be flattening the structure or expecting the fields to be named differently at the top level. Perhaps the API expects `tag` and `type` directly alongside `action` rather than nested inside `point`. Let me test passing them as top-level parameters instead."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6016, "output_tokens": 287, "latency_ms": 10655.665799975395, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The error message is confusing. Let me look at the schema again. The schema shows that `create_point` action expects parameters under \"point\" object with \"tag\" and \"type\" fields. But the error says \"create_point.tag: Field required\" which suggests it's looking for \"tag\" directly under the action object, not nested under \"point\". \n\nLet me check the exact schema structure. Looking at the JSON Schema for `create_point`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"action\": {\"const\": \"create_point\"},\n    \"point\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"tag\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"tag\", \"type\"],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"action\"],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n```\n\nWait, but the error says \"create_point.tag: Field required\" - this looks like it's checking at the top level for a \"tag\" field, not under \"point\". Maybe the schema is wrong or there's a validation issue. Let me try providing the fields at the top level."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6372, "output_tokens": 475, "latency_ms": 16682.563700014725, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I need to think about this differently. The error message says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\" - but I'm providing both tag and type. \n\nLooking at the schema again, for create_point action, the schema shows:\n- \"point\": {\"properties\": {\"tag\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"tag\", \"type\"], \"type\": \"object\"}\n\nBut wait, I see the issue. In the JSON schema, the \"point\" parameter is defined as a separate object that has tag and type. But when I call the function, I need to provide the \"point\" parameter as an object with tag and type inside it. But maybe the schema expects the point object to be provided differently?\n\nLet me look at the exact tool definition again:\n\nFor manage_points with create_point:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\", \n  \"title\": \"create_point\", \n  \"properties\": {\n    \"action\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"const\": \"create_point\"}, \n    \"point\": {\n      \"properties\": {\"tag\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \n      \"required\": [\"tag\", \"type\"], \n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  }, \n  \"required\": [\"action\"], \n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n```\n\nSo I need to provide:\n- action: \"create_point\"\n- point: {\"tag\": \"some_value\", \"type\": \"some_type\"}\n\nBut when I try that, it says field required. Let me try a different approach - maybe the error is misleading or there's something about the tool implementation. Let me try without the point wrapper, just tag and type directly.\n\nActually, looking at the error message format \"create_point.tag\" - this suggests it's looking for tag at the top level of create_point, not inside a point object. \n\nMaybe the schema description doesn't match the actual implementation. Let me try providing tag and type directly without the point wrapper."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6916, "output_tokens": 829, "latency_ms": 24258.809600025415, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I need to check the actual tool schema again. Looking at the tool definitions, for manage_points with create_point action, the schema is:\n\n```\n\"properties\": {\n  \"action\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"const\": \"create_point\"},\n  \"point\": {\n    \"properties\": {\"tag\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \n    \"required\": [\"tag\", \"type\"], \n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSo I need to pass a \"point\" object containing \"tag\" and \"type\". But the error message says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\", which suggests it's looking for tag and type at the top level. Let me try providing tag and type directly, not inside a point object. Actually, looking at the error more carefully: it says \"create_point.tag\" and \"create_point.type\", which implies it expects those as direct parameters, not nested.\n\nLet me try:\n- action: \"create_point\"\n- tag: \"T101\"\n- type: \"float\"\n\nBut the schema says point is required. Hmm. Maybe the error message is misleading. Let me try providing both the point object AND the direct parameters. Actually no, that would violate the schema.\n\nWait, maybe the issue is that I need to provide the point as a JSON string? No, the parameter expects an object. Let me look at the example in the instructions. The example shows:\n\n`<invoke name=\"example_complex_tool\">\n<parameter name=\"parameter\">[{\"color\": \"orange\", \"options\": {\"option_key_1\": true, \"option_key_2\": \"value\"}}, {\"color\": \"purple\", \"options\": {\"option_key_1\": true, \"option_key_2\": \"value\"}}]</parameter>\n</invoke>`\n\nSo the parameter should be the actual JSON object. Let me try:\n\n```json\n<invoke name=\"manage_points\">\n<parameter name=\"action\">create_point</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"point\">{\"tag\": \"T101\", \"type\": \"float\"}</parameter>\n</invoke>\n```\n\nBut I already tried that. The error says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\". This suggests the validation is checking for tag and type at the \"create_point\" level, not inside the point object. Maybe the schema I'm seeing is outdated or there's a bug. Let me try providing tag and type both inside the point object AND as top-level parameters.\n\nActually, looking at the schema more carefully: the schema for create_point shows:\n- action (required)\n- point (required) with properties tag and type (both required inside point)\n\nBut the error message format \"create_point.tag\" suggests it's looking for tag as a direct property of the create_point action. Maybe the schema is wrong or the validation is expecting a different structure.\n\nLet me try a different approach: maybe I need to provide the entire point object with all possible fields. The schema only shows tag and type, but maybe there are other required fields not shown? Let me try adding more fields like name, description, etc.\n\nActually, let me re-read the error: \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\". This is a validation error saying that at the \"create_point\" level, tag and type are required. So maybe the tool expects tag and type as direct parameters to the create_point action, not nested inside a point object.\n\nLet me try:\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"create_point\",\n  \"tag\": \"T101\",\n  \"type\": \"float\"\n}\n```\n\nBut that contradicts the schema. However, the error message is clear. Let me try this approach."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "DeploymentCheck"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 51533, "output_tokens": 5691, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 182522.9687000392}, "judge": null}
