create_point", "point": {"tag": "Temperature_T1", "type": "AI", "description": "反应釜温度"}}, "schema_valid": false, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "SCHEMA_ERROR", "error_msg": "create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 2.104699960909784, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}, {"turn": 12, "state": "CONFIG_POINT", "visible_tools": [{"name": "deployment", "allowed_actions": ["deploy_project", "show_deployment_status", "validate_project", "rollback_deployment"]}], "visible_count": 1, "selected": "deployment", "action": "show_deployment_status", "args": {"action": "show_deployment_status"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"deployment_id": "default", "status": "draft", "errors": []}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.3786000199615955, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": ["deployments.default"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:43d4f3e3424d08e6d0df74e774e92c960d43209e2c18f450ef8c3b2b7ba60734", "final_hash": "sha256:43d4f3e3424d08e6d0df74e774e92c960d43209e2c18f450ef8c3b2b7ba60734", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1635, "output_tokens": 631, "latency_ms": 18809.008400014136, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我来帮您完成反应釜综合监控方案的配置。不过，当前我在 **VALIDATE（验证）** 阶段，只能执行查询和验证操作，无法直接创建点位、画面和绑定操作。\n\n让我先为您全面排查当前项目状态，为后续配置做好准备：", "reasoning": "The user wants to create a comprehensive reactor monitoring solution with:\n1. New HMI page for reactor monitoring\n2. Three points: temperature, pressure, level\n3. Bind these points to widgets (tank and instruments) on the page\n4. Deploy and validate\n\nHowever, I'm currently in the VALIDATE stage, and the available tools are limited:\n- manage_pages: only allows list_pages\n- manage_history: only allows list_history\n- deployment: allows show_deployment_status, validate_project\n- manage_scripts: only allows list_scripts\n- manage_points: only allows list_points\n\nI cannot create pages, create points, bind widgets, or deploy with the current tools. The current stage only supports listing and validation operations.\n\nLet me think about what I can do:\n1. I can list existing pages, points, history, scripts to understand the current state\n2. I can validate the project\n3. I can show deployment status\n\nBut I cannot:\n- Create new pages\n- Create new points\n- Bind widgets to points\n- Deploy the project\n\nThe user's request involves creating new resources (pages, points, widget bindings) which requires actions not available in the current VALIDATE stage.\n\nAccording to my behavior guidelines:\n- \"若当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，你可以在回复的纯文本中包含 'next_state: 阶段名' 来切换到【可切换的下一阶段】中的合适阶段\"\n- The available next stages are: ANALYZE_INTENT, DEPLOY, DONE\n\nLooking at the workflow, this seems like a configuration task that needs ANALYZE_INTENT phase to properly understand and execute. Let me switch to ANALYZE_INTENT which likely has the tools needed for creating pages, points, and bindings.\n\nActually, wait - let me re-read the task. The user wants to:\n1. Create a new page\n2. Create 3 points\n\n\n3. Bind points to widgets\n4. Deploy and validate\n\nIn the current VALIDATE stage, I can only validate existing configurations. I should first check what currently exists, then switch to ANALYZE_INTENT to handle the configuration creation. I'll start by gathering information about the current project state - listing existing pages, points, scripts, and history to understand what's already configured before proceeding with the new setup."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1922, "output_tokens": 435, "latency_ms": 11744.412900006864, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "## 📊 当前项目状态排查结果\n\n| 项目 | 数量 | 状态 |\n|------|------|------|\n| 点位(Points) | 0 | 空项目 |\n| 画面(Pages) | 0 | 空项目 |\n| 历史归档(History) | 0 | 空项目 |\n| 脚本(Scripts) | 0 | 空项目 |\n\n---\n\n## 📋 您的反应釜监控方案需求梳理\n\n| 任务 | 详情 |\n|------|------|\n| 1️⃣ 新建画面 | 创建\"反应釜综合监控\"页面，包含储罐图形和仪表 |\n| 2️⃣ 新建点位 | `Temperature_T1` (温度)、`Pressure_P1` (压力)、`Level_L1` (液位) |\n| 3️⃣ 绑定关联 | 将点位绑定到画面中的罐体和仪表控件 |\n| 4️⃣ 验证下装 | 执行项目校验并部署 |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ 阶段切换说明\n\n当前 **VALIDATE 阶段**仅支持查询和验证操作，**无法执行创建点位、画面、控件绑定**等配置操作。\n\n我需要切换到 **ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段**，该阶段具备以下能力：\n- 创建/管理点位\n- 创建/管理画面和控件\n- 执行控件与点位的绑定\n- 部署和验证\n\nnext_state: ANALYZE_INTENT", "reasoning": "The project is empty - no points, no pages, no history, no scripts. This is a fresh project.\n\nNow I need to switch to the ANALYZE_INTENT stage which should have the tools needed to create points, pages, and widget bindings.\n\nAccording to my guidelines, I should include \"next_state: ANALYZE_INTENT\" to switch to the appropriate phase that can handle this configuration work."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2411, "output_tokens": 435, "latency_ms": 14529.105799971148, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，我现在进入 **ANALYZE_INTENT（意图分析）** 阶段。让我先获取当前项目部署状态，然后为您规划完整的配置流程。", "reasoning": "用户告诉我已进入 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段。让我查看当前可用的工具。\n\n根据系统提示，当前可用工具是：\n- deployment: Project validation, deployment, rollback, status.; 当前允许 actions: show_deployment_status, validate_project\n\n所以在 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段，我仍然只有 deployment 工具的 show_deployment_status 和 validate_project 两个 action。\n\n这仍然不足以完成用户的任务（创建点位、创建画面、绑定控件等）。\n\n让我先分析用户意图，然后可能需要切换到其他阶段。\n\n根据系统提示，可切换的下一阶段包括：\n- ASK_USER, BIND_POINTS, CONFIG_ALARM, CONFIG_HISTORY, CONFIG_POINT, CONFIG_SCRIPT, DEPLOY, DONE, GENERATE_LAYOUT, MANAGE_PAGES, VALIDATE\n\n要完成用户的任务：\n1. 创建点位 → 需要 CONFIG_POINT 阶段\n2. 创建画面 → 需要 MANAGE_PAGES 或 GENERATE_LAYOUT 阶段\n3. 绑定点位到控件 → 需要 BIND_POINTS 阶段\n4. 验证和部署 → 需要 VALIDATE 和 DEPLOY 阶段\n\n所以当前阶段（ANALYZE_INTENT）主要是用来分析意图，然后我应该：\n1. 先确认项目状态（使用 deployment 工具）\n2. 然后根据需要切换到合适的阶段\n\n让我先调用 show_deployment_status 了解当前项目状态，然后根据分析结果给出建议并切换到适当的阶段。\n\n\n用户的意图很明确，我应该先验证项目状态，然后逐步推荐工作流程。按照 CONFIG_POINT → MANAGE_PAGES → BIND_POINTS → VALIDATE → DEPLOY 的顺序依次切换阶段。先从查询项目状态开始。"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2915, "output_tokens": 542, "latency_ms": 15807.128300017212, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "## 📋 意图分析完成\n\n**项目状态**：`draft`（草稿态），无错误，可以进行配置。\n\n**用户需求解析**：\n\n| 步骤 | 任务 | 需要的阶段 |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| ① | 创建 3 个点位（温度、压力、液位） | `CONFIG_POINT` |\n| ② | 创建反应釜监控画面 | `MANAGE_PAGES` |\n| ③ | 设计画面布局（罐体、仪表） | `GENERATE_LAYOUT` |\n| ④ | 点位绑定到控件 | `BIND_POINTS` |\n| ⑤ | 项目验证 | `VALIDATE` |\n| ⑥ | 下装部署 | `DEPLOY` |\n\n---\n\n**建议执行顺序**：先创建点位（基础依赖），再创建画面和绑定，最后验证下装。\n\n接下来我将切换到 **CONFIG_POINT** 阶段，为您创建三个反应釜监控点位。\n\nnext_state: CONFIG_POINT", "reasoning": "用户要求我创建一个反应釜综合监控方案，包括：\n1. 新建画面\n2. 建三个点位（温度、压力、液位）\n3. 绑到画面的罐子和仪表上\n4. 最后下发验证\n\n当前在 ANALYZE_INTENT 阶段，可用工具只有 deployment，且只支持 show_deployment_status 和 validate_project。\n\n我已经确认项目状态是 draft，没有错误。\n\n现在需要切换到其他阶段来完成任务。根据可切换的下一阶段：\n- ASK_USER, BIND_POINTS, CONFIG_ALARM, CONFIG_HISTORY, CONFIG_POINT, CONFIG_SCRIPT, DEPLOY, DONE, GENERATE_LAYOUT, MANAGE_PAGES, VALIDATE\n\n要完成用户的任务，我需要：\n1. 创建点位 → CONFIG_POINT\n2. 创建画面/布局 → GENERATE_LAYOUT 或 MANAGE_PAGES\n3. 绑定点位到控件 → BIND_POINTS\n4. 验证 → VALIDATE\n5. 部署 → DEPLOY\n\n我应该先分析意图，然后告诉用户需要按什么顺序完成这些步骤，并切换到第一个需要的阶段。\n\n根据任务流程，合理的顺序是：\n1. CONFIG_POINT - 先创建点位\n2. MANAGE_PAGES / GENERATE_LAYOUT - 创建画面和布局\n3. BIND_POINTS - 绑定点位到控件\n4. VALIDATE - 验证\n\n\n5. DEPLOY - 部署\n\n先切换到 CONFIG_POINT 创建点位，因为这是基础依赖。"}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3471, "output_tokens": 663, "latency_ms": 16284.827099996619, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，现在进入 **CONFIG_POINT（点位配置）** 阶段。我来为反应釜监控方案创建三个工艺监测点位。", "reasoning": "用户已进入 CONFIG_POINT 阶段。让我查看当前可用的工具。\n\n根据系统提示，当前可用工具是：\n- manage_points: Create, update, delete, and list points. Currently allowed actions: list_points, create_point, update_point, delete_point, batch_update_points\n\n现在我可以创建点位了！我需要为反应釜监控方案创建三个点位：\n1. 温度点位 (Temperature)\n2. 压力点位 (Pressure)\n3. 液位点位 (Level)\n\n我需要参考之前的 schema 来创建合适的点位。让我设计这三个点位：\n\n1. 温度点位 - Temperature_T1\n   - name: \"Temperature_T1\"\n   - description: \"反应釜温度监测点\"\n   - type: \"AI\" (模拟量输入)\n   - dataType: \"float\" 或 \"REAL\"\n   - unit: \"°C\"\n   - address: 合适的地址\n\n2. 压力点位 - Pressure_P1\n   - name: \"Pressure_P1\"\n   - description: \"反应釜压力监测点\"\n   - type: \"AI\"\n   - dataType: \"float\" 或 \"REAL\"\n   - unit: \"MPa\" 或 \"kPa\"\n   - address: 合适的地址\n\n3. 液位点位 - Level_L1\n   - name: \"Level_L1\"\n   - description: \"反应釜液位监测点\"\n   - type: \"AI\"\n   - dataType: \"float\" 或 \"REAL\"\n   - unit: \"%\" 或 \"m\"\n   - address: 合适的地址\n\n这三个点位都是模拟量输入(AI)，用于监测反应釜的关键工艺参数。"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4274, "output_tokens": 323, "latency_ms": 5166.823100007605, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "收到，点位创建需要 `tag` 和 `type` 字段。让我调整参数重新创建：", "reasoning": "The schema requires \"tag\" and \"type\" fields. Let me adjust the point creation to use the correct field names. It seems \"tag\" is used instead of \"name\", and \"type\" is required. Let me try again with the correct schema."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4737, "output_tokens": 289, "latency_ms": 8803.73270000564, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我仔细查看点位创建的 schema，使用正确的字段结构：", "reasoning": "The schema is still rejecting my requests. Let me look at the function definition more carefully:\n\n```\n\"create_point\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"title\": \"Description\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"enabled\": {\"default\": true, \"title\": \"Enabled\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"name\": {\"title\": \"Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"title\": \"Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"name\", \"type\"], \"title\": \"create_point\", \"type\": \"object\"}\n```\n\nSo the required fields are \"name\" and \"type\". The \"tag\" field doesn't exist in this schema - it uses \"name\" instead. Let me try again with the correct field names: name and type.\n\nThe error message says \"create_point.tag: Field required\" which is confusing because the schema says \"name\" is required, not \"tag\". Maybe the error message is misleading.\n\nLet me try with the exact schema structure - using \"name\" and \"type\" as required fields."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5092, "output_tokens": 387, "latency_ms": 11011.239300016314, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "错误提示需要 `tag` 和 `type` 字段。让我尝试将这些字段直接放在顶层参数：", "reasoning": "The schema error says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\". This is confusing because the schema definition shows \"name\" and \"type\" as required fields, not \"tag\".\n\nLet me look at the parameter structure more carefully. The action is passed at the top level, not inside the point object. Let me try restructuring - maybe \"tag\" and \"type\" need to be at the top level alongside \"action\", not nested inside a \"point\" object.\n\nLooking at the schema again:\n```\n\"create_point\": {\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"action\": {\"const\": \"create_point\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"point\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"name\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"enabled\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"name\", \"type\"],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"action\", \"point\"]\n}\n```\n\nWait, the error says \"create_point.tag\" not \"create_point.point.tag\". Maybe the expected structure is different from what I'm seeing. Let me try putting tag and type directly at the root level:\n\n```\n{\n  \"action\": \"create_point\",\n  \"tag\": \"Temperature_T1\",\n  \"type\": \"AI\"\n}\n```\n\nThis might be a case where the actual API expects different fields than what's documented in the schema. Let me try this approach."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5545, "output_tokens": 588, "latency_ms": 16595.58200003812, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试在 point 对象中同时包含 `tag` 字段：", "reasoning": "Still getting the same error. Let me think about this differently. The error message says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\". \n\nMaybe I need to look at the schema more carefully. The function definition shows the schema for all actions, but when I call \"create_point\", it's looking for specific fields.\n\nLooking at the original schema definition again:\n```\n\"create_point\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"title\": \"Description\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"enabled\": {\"default\": true, \"title\": \"Enabled\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"name\": {\"title\": \"Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"title\": \"Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"name\", \"type\"], \"title\": \"create_point\", \"type\": \"object\"}\n```\n\nWait, the error says \"tag\" is required but the schema says \"name\" is required. This is contradictory.\n\nMaybe the point object needs to include both \"tag\" and \"type\" explicitly. Let me try with a point object that has both fields:\n\nActually, wait - I've been trying this. Let me look at how I'm passing parameters.\n\nWhen I call:\n```\n<invoke name=\"manage_points\">\n<parameter name=\"action\">create_point</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"point\">{\"name\": \"Temperature_T1\", \"type\": \"AI\"}</parameter>\n</invoke>\n```\n\nThe tool receives action=\"create_point\" and point={\"name\": \"Temperature_T1\", \"type\": \"AI\"}.\n\nBut the error says \"create_point.tag: Field required\" - this suggests the tool is looking for a \"tag\" field within the \"create_point\" action context, not within the \"point\" object.\n\nMaybe the structure should be different. Let me try passing \"tag\" and \"type\" as direct parameters to the point object, since that's what seems to be expected based on the error message.\n\n\nThe schema explicitly lists \"name\" as required, not \"tag\", yet the error keeps mentioning \"tag\". This mismatch suggests I might need to pass both fields or the tool has a different expectation than what the schema documents. Let me test including \"tag\" alongside \"name\" in the point object to see if that satisfies the validation."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6199, "output_tokens": 378, "latency_ms": 11037.347199977376, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我简化 point 对象，只保留核心必填字段：", "reasoning": "I'm still getting the same error. This is very strange. Let me look at the function definition again:\n\n```\n\"manage_points\": {\n  \"parameters\": {\n    \"oneOf\": [\n      {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"action\": {\"const\": \"list_points\"},\n          ...\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"action\": {\"const\": \"create_point\"},\n          \"point\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n              \"enabled\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"},\n              \"name\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n              \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"name\", \"type\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"action\", \"point\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe schema clearly says \"name\" and \"type\" are required, not \"tag\". But the error says \"tag\" is required.\n\nWait, maybe I need to look at this differently. The error message format \"create_point.tag\" suggests that \"tag\" is being looked up at the action level, not inside the point object.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - what if the parameter name should be \"tag\" instead of \"name\" in the actual implementation, despite what the schema says?\n\nActually, I've already tried including \"tag\" in the point object and it still failed.\n\nLet me try making \"tag\" and \"type\" the ONLY fields in the point object, removing everything else:"}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6643, "output_tokens": 566, "latency_ms": 15425.788900000043, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我确认一下当前工具的实际调用结构。我尝试不使用嵌套对象，直接传参：", "reasoning": "I keep getting the same error. Let me think about this differently.\n\nThe error message says \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\"\n\nThis error format \"create_point.tag\" could mean that the tool is looking for these fields at a different level than I'm providing them.\n\nLooking at the schema again for create_point:\n```\n{\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"action\": {\"const\": \"create_point\"},\n    \"point\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"enabled\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"},\n        \"name\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"type\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"name\", \"type\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"action\", \"point\"]\n}\n```\n\nWait - I just realized something. The schema says \"point\" object has \"name\" and \"type\" as required. But the error says \"tag\" is required.\n\nMaybe there's a mismatch between what the schema documents and what the actual API expects. \n\nLet me try one more thing - what if I need to pass the parameters in a completely different structure? What if instead of a nested \"point\" object, I should pass \"tag\" and \"type\" as direct parameters?\n\nActually, I already tried that and it didn't work either.\n\nLet me look at the actual XML I'm generating... When I call:\n```\n<invoke name=\"manage_points\">\n<parameter name=\"action\">create_point</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"point\">{\"tag\": \"Temperature_T1\", \"name\": \"Temperature_T1\", \"type\": \"AI\"}</parameter>\n</invoke>\n```\n\nThis should pass action=\"create_point\" and point={\"tag\": \"Temperature_T1\", \"name\": \"Temperature_T1\", \"type\": \"AI\"} to the tool.\n\nBut the error suggests the tool isn't receiving \"tag\" and \"type\" in the point object.\n\n\nI'm wondering if there's a schema definition mismatch - the error message references \"tag\" as required, but the schema I'm looking at lists \"name\" instead. This could indicate the actual API expects different fields than what's documented. Let me try passing \"tag\" and \"type\" directly as top-level parameters instead of nested within the point object, though I may have attempted this before without success."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7275, "output_tokens": 536, "latency_ms": 9730.647499964107, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我遇到持续的 schema 错误。让我尝试一种不同的方式——也许需要查看工具的完整 schema 结构：", "reasoning": "I keep getting the same error no matter what I try. The error message \"create_point.tag: Field required; create_point.type: Field required\" is consistent.\n\nLet me re-examine the schema one more time:\n\n```\n\"create_point\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"title\": \"Description\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"enabled\": {\"default\": true, \"title\": \"Enabled\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"name\": {\"title\": \"Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": {\"title\": \"Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"name\", \"type\"], \"title\": \"create_point\", \"type\": \"object\"}\n```\n\nWait a minute... I just realized something. The schema shows that the \"point\" parameter has these fields: description, enabled, name, type. And it requires \"name\" and \"type\".\n\nBut the error says \"tag\" is required, not \"name\". This is very strange.\n\nCould it be that the error message is incorrect or misleading? Or could it be that the actual implementation expects different fields than what the schema documents?\n\nLet me try one more thing - what if I need to pass the point data without the \"point\" wrapper? What if the tool expects the point fields to be at the same level as \"action\"?\n\nActually, looking at the schema structure more carefully:\n```\n\"oneOf\": [\n  {\"title\": \"list_points\", ...},\n  {\"title\": \"create_point\", \"properties\": {\"action\": {...}, \"point\": {...}}, \"required\": [\"action\", \"point\"]},\n  ...\n]\n```\n\nThe \"create_point\" schema requires both \"action\" and \"point\" at the top level. And the \"point\" object requires \"name\" and \"type\".\n\nI've been doing this correctly all along. \n\nSomething's preventing the tool from accepting these fields. Let me consider whether the implementation itself might have a bug or if there's an undocumented requirement. The error message format \"create_point.tag\" suggests the validation is looking for \"tag\" at the action's root level, but the schema explicitly shows \"name\" as the required field instead. I should verify whether I'm actually transmitting the data correctly—let me check if my JSON formatting in the point parameter might be the issue."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "DeploymentCheck"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 52119, "output_tokens": 5773, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 155051.96759995306}, "judge": null}
