dband": "0.0", "priority": "medium"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "ALREADY_EXISTS", "error_msg": "alarm alarm_pt101_high already exists", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.6257000000005064, "intended_entities": ["alarms.alarm_pt101_high"], "referenced_entities": ["points.PT101"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:e2c29cbc7447c81385d26f1579bf0aed934b95ee41882b9350d4f7775d3027a7", "final_hash": null, "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 967, "output_tokens": 131, "latency_ms": 8018.090900000061, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想要为PT101配置高限报警，阈值2.0，中等优先级。当前阶段是ANALYZE_INTENT，可用工具有manage_pages和manage_points。这两个工具都不直接支持配置报警。要配置报警，可能需要进入CONFIG_ALARM阶段。不过，我首先需要确认PT101点是否存在。我可以先调用manage_points来列出所有点，或者过滤查找PT101。让我先列出所有点，看看PT101是否存在。"}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2024, "output_tokens": 300, "latency_ms": 7462.258199999951, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户现在进入了 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段。当前可用的工具有 manage_alarms 和 manage_points（仅 list_points 操作）。用户要求为 PT101 配置高限报警，阈值 2.0，中等优先级。PT101 是一个模拟量点，类型为 analog。我需要为这个点创建一个模拟量报警（analog alarm），动作是 create_analog_alarm。需要提供 id、tag、high_limit、deadband、priority 等参数。id 可以自定义，比如 \"alarm_pt101_high\"。deadband 可以设为 0.0，或者询问用户。但用户没有指定 deadband，我可以使用默认值 0.0。priority 是 \"medium\"。high_limit 是 2.0。low_limit 不需要，设为 null。那么调用 manage_alarms 工具，action 为 create_analog_alarm。现在执行。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2398, "output_tokens": 120, "latency_ms": 3298.787700000048, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The error says low_limit should be a valid number, not null. Let me try without specifying low_limit at all, since it's optional (has default null)."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3784, "output_tokens": 160, "latency_ms": 4963.142300000072, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "It seems the tool has an issue with null values. Let me try passing 0 as the low_limit since the user only wants a high limit alarm. Or maybe I should pass a very low number like -9999 to effectively disable the low limit. Let me try passing 0 for low_limit."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4018, "output_tokens": 173, "latency_ms": 4566.879500000141, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The error persists. It seems the tool is having trouble parsing the low_limit parameter. Let me check if the parameter is being passed correctly. The schema says low_limit should be a number or null. Let me try passing it as a string \"0\" instead. Or maybe I need to explicitly pass it as null. Let me try without low_limit again, but this time make sure I'm not accidentally including it. Let me also check if the issue is with how I'm passing the parameters. Let me try a simpler approach."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4265, "output_tokens": 278, "latency_ms": 8040.170499999931, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "There seems to be a schema error with the low_limit parameter. Even when I don't provide it, the tool is complaining about it. Let me try a different approach - maybe I need to provide all parameters explicitly. Let me try using Python number literals without quotes.\n\nWait, looking at the schema again:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nThe default is null, so I shouldn't need to provide it. But it keeps failing. Let me try providing it as a number explicitly. The error says \"unable to parse string as a number\" which suggests the value is being passed as a string somehow.\n\nLet me try passing low_limit as a very low number like -999999 to effectively disable it."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4617, "output_tokens": 143, "latency_ms": 5113.6103999999705, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I need to figure out the correct way to pass a null value for low_limit. The schema says it accepts number or null with default null. Let me try different approaches. Maybe I should explicitly pass it as null in JSON format."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4835, "output_tokens": 243, "latency_ms": 6095.3133000000435, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我注意到系统在处理 `low_limit` 参数时出现了问题。让我尝试不包含该参数：", "reasoning": "I'm having trouble with the low_limit parameter. The error says it's trying to parse a string as a number. Let me look at the schema more carefully:\n\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n\nSo it should accept either a number or null. Let me try not including it at all since it has a default of null. But when I tried that, it still gave the same error. \n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe the JSON needs to be formatted differently. I should try to not include the low_limit parameter at all."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5152, "output_tokens": 179, "latency_ms": 5264.474500000006, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool seems to have a bug where it's not properly handling the null value for low_limit. Let me try a different approach - perhaps I should create a digital alarm or try with different parameter combinations. Or maybe I should set the low_limit to a very low number like -99999.\n\nLet me try once more with a negative number for low_limit."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 32060, "output_tokens": 1727, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 54466.337199999994}, "judge": null}
