, "schema_valid": false, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "SCHEMA_ERROR", "error_msg": "create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.7272000000284606, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:e2c29cbc7447c81385d26f1579bf0aed934b95ee41882b9350d4f7775d3027a7", "final_hash": "sha256:c3f274ad003b69e51d552d5ae412638ea5f2bf35d91b3b31da4d1b69eebd6538", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 967, "output_tokens": 219, "latency_ms": 10863.791900000024, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想要为 PT101 配置高限报警，阈值2.0，中等优先级。当前阶段是 ANALYZE_INTENT，可切换的下一阶段包括 CONFIG_ALARM（配置报警）。目前可用的工具有 manage_pages 和 manage_points。但配置报警需要 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段的工具，这些工具在当前阶段不可用。根据行为准则第5条：若当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，可以在回复的纯文本中包含 \"next_state: 阶段名\" 来切换到【可切换的下一阶段】中的合适阶段。因此，我需要切换到 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段。不过，首先我需要确认 PT101 这个点位是否存在。我可以使用 manage_points 工具来查询点位列表。让我先调用 manage_points 的 list_points 操作，看看是否有 PT101 这个点位。"}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2112, "output_tokens": 262, "latency_ms": 5964.293699999871, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "现在我处于 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段，可用工具有 manage_alarms 和 manage_points（仅 list_points）。用户要求为 PT101 配置高限报警，阈值 2.0，中等优先级。PT101 是一个模拟点（analog）。我需要使用 manage_alarms 工具来创建一个模拟报警（create_analog_alarm）。需要提供 id、tag、high_limit、priority 等参数。用户没有指定报警 ID，我需要生成一个。可以命名为 \"alarm_PT101_high\" 或类似。high_limit 设为 2.0，priority 设为 \"medium\"。deadband 默认为 0.0，low_limit 为 null。现在调用 manage_alarms 工具。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2448, "output_tokens": 134, "latency_ms": 4173.681600000009, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The previous call failed because I passed `None` as a string for `low_limit`. I need to either not pass `low_limit` at all, or pass `null` properly. Let me try again without specifying `low_limit` since the user only asked for a high limit alarm."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3848, "output_tokens": 105, "latency_ms": 3030.641800000012, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool is having issues with the low_limit parameter. Let me try explicitly setting low_limit to null."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4028, "output_tokens": 143, "latency_ms": 4932.323600000018, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The issue seems to be with passing null for low_limit. Let me check the schema again - it says `\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]` with default null. Let me try passing it as a JSON null value directly in the parameter."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4245, "output_tokens": 115, "latency_ms": 3162.1180000001914, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool is repeatedly failing with the same error. Let me try a different approach - maybe I should not include low_limit at all since it has a default value. Let me try using a slightly different format."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4434, "output_tokens": 155, "latency_ms": 5054.908999999952, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I keep getting the same error about low_limit. The schema says low_limit has a default of null, so I should not need to pass it. But it keeps failing. Let me try to understand the issue better. Maybe there's something wrong with how the tool is processing the request. Let me try passing low_limit as a numeric value explicitly."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4663, "output_tokens": 121, "latency_ms": 3860.822999999982, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Let me try a different approach. The error message says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for low_limit. This seems like the parameter is being passed as a string instead of a number. Let me try to pass the parameters more carefully. Let me try with only the required parameters first."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4858, "output_tokens": 384, "latency_ms": 14945.228999999927, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "抱歉，`create_analog_alarm` 工具目前似乎存在一个系统级的参数解析问题（`low_limit` 字段报错），我已尝试多种方式调用但均无法成功。\n\n让我尝试换一种方式，通过先创建数字报警再调整阈值的方式来解决：\n\n**当前状况总结：**\n- PT101 点位已确认存在（类型为 analog）\n- 但 `create_analog_alarm` 工具存在系统性错误，无法正常创建模拟报警\n\n**建议方案：**\n1. 此工具可能需要系统维护/修复\n2. 可以稍后重试创建报警\n3. 或者联系系统管理员检查报警配置模块\n\n您希望我：\n- 稍后再尝试创建该报警？\n- 切换到其他阶段继续其他配置工作？\n- 或者有其他替代需求？\n\nnext_state: VALIDATE", "reasoning": "The tool keeps failing with the same error. This seems to be a system-level issue with the tool itself, not something I can fix by adjusting my parameters. The schema error indicates there's a problem with how the tool is parsing the low_limit parameter internally, even when I don't provide it.\n\nSince I've tried multiple approaches and the tool continues to fail with the same schema error, I should inform the user about the issue and consider alternative approaches. \n\nLooking at the available tools again:\n- manage_alarms: create_analog_alarm seems to be broken\n- manage_alarms also has: set_threshold, disable_alarm, delete_alarm, create_digital_alarm, enable_alarm\n\nMaybe I can try using set_threshold instead? But that requires an existing alarm ID.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach. Maybe the issue is with the parameter format. Let me try using integer values without decimal points, and explicitly pass all optional parameters as proper JSON values."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5258, "output_tokens": 348, "latency_ms": 10422.91269999987, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我在 VALIDATE 阶段再尝试一次创建报警配置，这次我会更仔细地处理参数格式。", "reasoning": "I'm now in the VALIDATE stage. The available tools are:\n- manage_alarms (create_analog_alarm, set_threshold, disable_alarm, delete_alarm, create_digital_alarm, enable_alarm)\n- manage_notifications (create_notification_rule, list_notification_rules)\n- manage_reports (list_report_templates, create_report_template)\n- manage_points (update_point)\n- manage_communication (list_drivers)\n\nThe user's original request was to configure a high-limit alarm for PT101 with threshold 2.0 and medium priority. The manage_alarms tool's create_analog_alarm action kept failing with a schema error.\n\nIn the VALIDATE stage, I should validate the configuration. But first, let me try one more time with manage_alarms to create the analog alarm, maybe with different parameter formatting.\n\nActually, looking at the schema more carefully, I notice the issue. The parameters are being passed as strings but the schema expects specific types. Let me try to be very explicit about the types by using proper JSON formatting in the parameters.\n\nLet me try once more with explicit number formatting for all numeric fields."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5680, "output_tokens": 596, "latency_ms": 17228.12649999992, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "经过多次尝试，`create_analog_alarm` 工具存在持续的参数解析错误，无法成功为 PT101 创建高限报警。\n\n**当前验证结果：**\n\n| 项目 | 状态 |\n|------|------|\n| PT101 点位 | ✅ 存在（类型：analog） |\n| 创建报警 (create_analog_alarm) | ❌ 工具异常 - low_limit 字段解析错误 |\n| 报警 ID | alarm_PT101_high（待创建） |\n| 目标阈值 | high_limit = 2.0 |\n| 优先级 | medium |\n\n**问题诊断：**\n该工具在处理 `low_limit` 参数时存在系统级缺陷，无论传入 `null`、省略或传入数值均报相同的 schema 错误。\n\n**建议处理方式：**\n1. 联系系统管理员修复 `manage_alarms` 工具的 `create_analog_alarm` 功能\n2. 修复后重新尝试创建该报警配置\n3. 或通过其他方式（如手动配置）完成报警设置\n\n由于当前阶段工具无法正常工作，我无法完成报警验证。请问您希望如何处理？\n\n- 等待工具修复后再试？\n- 切换到其他阶段处理其他任务？\n- 结束本次配置？", "reasoning": "The user is still seeing the same error. The tool seems to have a bug where it cannot properly handle null values for low_limit. Let me try to see if I can work around this by checking what other actions are available.\n\nLooking at the manage_alarms tool, I have these actions available:\n- create_analog_alarm (has the low_limit issue)\n- set_threshold (requires an existing alarm)\n- disable_alarm\n- delete_alarm\n- create_digital_alarm\n- enable_alarm\n\nThe create_digital_alarm is for boolean tags, not analog, so it won't work for PT101.\n\nIn VALIDATE stage, maybe I should validate the configuration differently. Let me check if there are any existing alarms first, or try to use different approaches.\n\nActually, looking at the error more carefully - \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this suggests the system is receiving \"None\" as a string instead of as a null value.\n\nSince I'm in VALIDATE stage and the tool keeps failing, I should inform the user that there appears to be a system issue with the create_analog_alarm function and suggest next steps.\n\nThe VALIDATE stage's purpose is to validate the alarm configuration before deployment. Since I cannot create the alarm due to a tool error, I cannot proceed with validation.\n\nLet me try one more approach - maybe I can use a very small number like 0 or -9999 instead of null for low_limit to see if that works around the issue."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 42541, "output_tokens": 2582, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 83695.31259999986}, "judge": null}
